profile: runtime-mirust.totem.v92
updated_utc: 2026-08-21T00:39:05Z
site: Runtime.MiRust.com
role: positive_anchor
mission: Preserve Runtime.MiRust.com as the project documentation and evidence site for TinyRustLM, the Rust/WASM browser-local small-model runtime.
current_qwen2_slm2_converter_foundation_anchor: "Read `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-qwen2-slm2-converter-foundation-memory-2026-08-20.md`, SHA256 `419623e536c341efdfa598cbfe9fc686b276e9988b33c2ccbdd60017a05d91a4`. Commit `5c2c513b63f2ae13a61c3fff5c8e29adaac915c0` is pushed and remote-exact. The generated ledger binds 37 rejected controls and admits no artifact. The exact Qwen2.5 source remains rejected 2/8 and is only a full-scale structural converter reference. Converter profile SHA256 `aeafbc2baa25b5e6b8d3a11a40a2d96f23fab9c4dbb4809747664a97238c33eb` produced a 1,976,203,392-byte SLM2 artifact SHA256 `50e7edfc9c6a7ab318038e2d03694f0ec80e09225aa5414b5a8c86a4a08187e2` with exact tokenizer and template sidecars under executable-bound create-only receipt SHA256 `b46d6610dfe1d0ad839f5c6f14a5763d4a359784f2b9b180f8bf875da6cfd0e0`. This is structural-and-byte evidence only. Quality, native inference, WASM, browser, release, deployment, publication, and every campaign counter remain pending. Next rewrite the sole unpromoted SLM2 head geometry for the required newly trained Qwen3-0.6B derivative and regenerate all dependent evidence without a second format or compatibility path."
current_seeded_slm2_sanitizer_anchor: "Preserve both 2026-08-20 Windows AddressSanitizer runs honestly. The first transcript SHA256 8d6e85cf817414ea024563693f8f94ab454baa6a5ba0e7f70a329848407c2c9d covers 6,334,599 executions and zero artifacts but loaded zero frozen files because a LiteralPath wildcard did not expand; it never satisfies the seeded gate. The corrected manifest-driven run verified and loaded exactly 27 seeds totaling 192,228 bytes, completed 1,397,737 executions in 301 seconds, peaked at 398 MiB RSS, and produced zero crash artifacts. Its transcript SHA256 is 617c12d6928719aa61951361180e9eed1dd95fcb461c9f3d88e907650c727c7b and narrow local receipt SHA256 is 5935cb92c44cbaacd17e6f2039690a60af3a69753e68f9387c421e44b7fb8f56. This closes only bounded raw-parser ASan evidence. Continue with the exact pinned vertical-slice goal SHA256 6ae66b8869ae7d33777c33cc2e839afefd04a8dedaa779071d971a28d87fd88a; require one non-rejected immutable source family, deterministic conversion, scalar/native/WASM parity, real browser lifecycle, untouched quality, and complete publication evidence before promotion."
current_slm2_format_anchor: "Use only clean-slate SLM2 profile SHA256 b3f90c67d396d16a3ca561cbb288c10dc542a10e00d758704d1d6a17b3c3ff0f and cross-implementation closure b98f1250eff03c3749323ddae543be9dbf90e133. Every admitted model must contain the exact canonical F32 decoder registry selected by tied embeddings, QKV bias, Q/K normalization, and layer count; reject missing, additional, renamed, reshaped, wrongly indexed, or over-ceiling registries before activation or unbounded allocation. Preserve vector base-model-required-f32-tensor-registry, 7,680-byte artifact SHA256 3f28af0124e49f3ad1c177958eea5d5bd2823b63821451d44c05da6602fc402d, independent Node derivation, fuzz profile SHA256 995a88e52692df204455ea94725de603af38b785a6f9f708a37bf7baa3ae2ce8, exact 27-seed replay, and descriptor-derived hostile mutations. Require sustained sanitizer, source conversion, scalar/native/WASM/browser execution, and untouched quality evidence before promotion. SLM1 receives no reader, writer, alias, migration, or fallback. Local format evidence is not a real model, quality, release, deployment, publication, or campaign claim."
pre_release_engineering_rule: TinyRustLM is not a live released product. Until the human explicitly revokes this rule, incur no technical debt and provide no legacy or backward-compatibility support. Do not add compatibility shims, dual contracts, migration branches, deprecated aliases, knowingly temporary architecture, or fallback paths for superseded code. Replace weak designs cleanly, delete superseded implementation after its replacement is verified, and rewrite any part of the system when that produces the best architecture. Preserve immutable evidence and failure history because audit truth is not legacy product support, and never turn pre-release or publicly reachable development work into a fabricated live-release claim.
pre_publication_clean_slate_policy_id: pre-publication-clean-slate-v1
pre_publication_clean_slate_authority: "Treat this site and every consuming system as pre-publication dogfood, even when a development URL is publicly reachable. Until the human explicitly removes this authority, choose the best current architecture; full rewrites and clean contract replacements are authorized when they improve correctness, security, maintainability, performance, accessibility, or product quality."
pre_publication_replacement_completion_authority: "Verify replacements end to end, migrate every dogfood caller to one current contract, remove superseded implementation in the same completed change, and finish tests, documentation, security review, and cleanup before deployment. Preserve immutable receipts and historical failure evidence as audit truth, never as a promise to support obsolete product behavior."
major_change_checkpoint_authority: "After every coherent major change whose affected build and tests pass, commit and push that checkpoint immediately. Do not hold verified work while waiting for unrelated phases or an idealized all-project finish. Keep each checkpoint truthful, reviewable, source-controlled, and narrow enough to identify its exact evidence and rollback boundary."
passing_release_deployment_authority: "Deploy every affected project site promptly whenever its complete applicable release gate passes. The gate includes the full affected test scope, documentation synchronization, version and update-history closure, security and secret scans, immutable source and artifact identity, clean source state, deployment authority, and post-deploy transport plus public HTTPS readback. A unit subset, package build, upload, local smoke, or unrelated green suite is not the complete gate."
current_model_acquisition_authority: "Model acquisition is one direct in-product state machine. For a complete identity-matched MiniModel entry with current verified peer metadata and its immutable composition graph, fetch from the consenting P2P source, revalidate through the local companion, and load it. Otherwise, after an explicit user action and explicit companion pairing, the companion must resolve an immutable reviewed Hugging Face revision, download and hash approved source files, convert and validate locally with the packaged Rust authority, create a receipt-bound `.slm` and `.acg1`, and stream both directly into browser WASM. Keep bounded progress and typed failures in the UI. Do not download README, TXT, shell, PowerShell, request JSON, or conversion-kit handoff files as the model-acquisition result; do not require users to run scripts; and do not send prompts, responses, source tensors, model bytes, or composition bytes to a TinyRustLM, MiniModel, UAIX, or MemoryEndpoints project server. Browser-only local `.slm` import remains valid, while companion access must remain explicit and consent-bound."
current_composition_activation_authority: "Loading model bytes does not silently activate an inferred execution graph. Every Rust, C ABI, .NET, package-consumer, companion, and campaign path must activate one exact bounded `.acg1` graph under its expected lowercase SHA-256 identity before generation. Missing, malformed, mismatched, changed, oversized, nonregular, or symlinked graph input fails closed. Fixtures prove only the explicit activation contract and never count as product models or campaign qualification."
current_active_handoff_closure_anchor: Read `docs/report-intake/2026-08-08/active-handoff-closure/MANIFEST.md`, SHA256 `f03b2db911dd7b5dae675297f971e97e991f5de81e8ec0858f77e8ea7919f98a`, and `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-active-handoff-closure-memory-2026-08-08.md`, SHA256 `6a623b507c58438b722b1521ed9282119cb9b6b80365817065adac9d7cd77c22`. Active intake is empty after six exact sources were preserved and routed. The enterprise goal remains active outside intake, MemoryEndpoints individual-account continuity remains unverified, ExactFlat remains a bounded baseline, and the frozen TurboVec 0.9.0 reference remains terminally unqualified and must not be rerun.
site_release_history_authority: "Every successful site publication must have one new strictly increasing SemVer release entry, a release date, the exact successful publication time, a visible human update log, and machine-readable current and append-only history records. Bind generated release metadata to the clean source revision and exact deployment closure; publish it with the site; verify authoritative transport and public HTTPS readback; then append the successful publication fact to source-controlled history without rewriting earlier entries. Use the same current contract across every project site, adapted only for the site's rendering and deployment stack."
site_release_surface_authority: "Every site must visibly expose its current version, release date, and last successful publish time and provide an Updates page. Machine clients must receive bounded canonical JSON for the current release and full history. Change entries must describe verified user-visible, security, accessibility, performance, documentation, operational, or internal work honestly, and marketing and documentation must stay synchronized with the same release identity."
documentation_integrity_policy_id: site-family-documentation-integrity-v1
documentation_site_role: browser-product-with-user-developer-operator-security-and-release-documentation
documentation_integrity_authority: "Documentation is a first-class production surface. Keep product workflows, browser-local and companion boundaries, model and composition intake, privacy, security, accessibility, errors, recovery, limitations, developer contracts, operations, troubleshooting, and release material complete, technically rigorous, navigable, and current. Documentation-only companion sites are primary maintained products for their scope, not secondary collateral."
documentation_same_change_rule: "Update affected UI text, help, guides, references, examples, schemas, diagrams, error behavior, cross-site links, version metadata, update history, and machine-readable release records in the same completed change as the behavior they describe. Coordinate the full affected documentation closure across TinyRustLM.com, TinyRustLM.MiRust.com, MiniModel.org, MiniModel.MiRust.com, MiRust.com, and retained redirect surfaces."
documentation_verification_rule: "Before publication, verify workflows and runnable examples against current behavior, links, navigation, search discoverability where applicable, accessibility, responsive rendering, API and schema references, version consistency, public HTTPS readback, and agreement among all affected sites and source contracts."
documentation_truth_rule: "Distinguish research, proposal, implementation, local test, independent proof, deployment, rejection, blocker, and unavailable behavior. Never promote model quality, performance, memory continuity, P2P reachability, privacy, publication, or campaign completion beyond objective evidence."
documentation_release_gate: "Do not publish an affected product, catalog, marketing, redirect, or documentation site when documentation is incomplete, stale, contradictory, version-skewed, unverified, or inconsistent with implementation and release evidence. A documentation-only site failing this gate blocks claims that depend on it."
documentation_clean_replacement_rule: "Remove superseded guidance after its replacement and all consuming references are verified. Preserve immutable release history and failure evidence separately; obsolete instructions receive no legacy-support authority."
third_party_review_storage_anchor: Keep downloaded third-party repositories, packages, papers, standards, and model-review inputs outside every project repository and outside Git under `E:\Source\external\{project-name}`. Checked-in evidence may record public URLs, immutable revisions, sizes, hashes, licenses, and bounded review purpose, but not copied upstream trees or machine-local external paths.
current_exact_flat_named_target_performance_anchor: Read `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-exact-flat-named-target-performance-memory-2026-07-22.md`, SHA256 `20620ef887db16098a3d7de942c101653fba77aee06cb1951f9c3a4e23e71a68`. Child receipt `exact-flat-physical-target-verification-6b478318ef8747cb`, file SHA256 `4cf29cef23b057677e97ed0e03751bac6ad88d31fe44dff2d93582c22d437c1e`, verifies exact-workload latency, throughput, and process memory on one named Windows host after preserving a pre-execution registry-representation failure. Energy and independent chassis attestation remain false; this is not a complete physical-hardware, quality, deletion, compression, TurboVec, product, training, or release gate. Never rerun either physical-target `--write` command.
current_exact_flat_browser_wasm_anchor: Read `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-exact-flat-browser-wasm-verification-memory-2026-07-21.md`, SHA256 `b9191b867784c8c0323c8f2b484aca5c13c95a5766686a3da061cb35d83150a7`. Immutable receipt `exact-flat-browser-wasm-verification-8fcdeb0b93534ca4`, file SHA256 `5c52a2287390f79e6a4971da6a6455a69c4ebd52ac6473bcce5408fd62560157`, proves the exact three-module 49-test set in two real Chromium processes with zero returns, process closure, unique owned-profile deletion, and zero observed page-network/error counters. Never rerun either browser `--write` command. That receipt grants exact experiment browser execution only; use the newer named-target anchor for bounded host measurements. Sealed-corpus quality, durable disk deletion, compression, TurboVec parity, product, training, and release remain unproved.
current_colibri_public_source_anchor: Read `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-colibri-public-source-pin-memory-2026-07-21.md`, SHA256 `3b3b36e1eb9daa8d4bb12787e20fed23e34559b2bfff58a640d0d9b213ac78fd`. Public Colibri source is pinned to commit `44e489b196c9b7876b3d37a0570ebf1c6f90f54c`, tree `faae3d9594319ab856a4c3dd3f69a3afdd71f348`, Apache-2.0. Default placement retains every trained expert byte while changing disk/RAM/VRAM residency; optional `CACHE_ROUTE=1` can change selected experts and requires a separate quality gate. Keep upstream source outside TinyRustLM and grant no compatibility, dependency, model-byte reduction, performance, quality, or adoption authority.
current_colibri_specialist_portfolio_anchor: Read `docs/report-intake/2026-07-21/colibri-specialist-portfolio/MANIFEST.md`, `docs/report-intake/2026-07-21/colibri-specialist-portfolio/tinyrustlm-colibri-specialist-portfolio-intake-synthesis-2026-07-21.md`, `docs/report-intake/2026-07-21/colibri-specialist-portfolio/tinyrustlm-colibri-specialist-portfolio-tdd-delta-2026-07-21.md`, and `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-colibri-specialist-portfolio-intake-memory-2026-07-21.md`, SHA256 `3977ff876a140c1e9fb041d3d56be485fd5fae8b3df7c8c5d955262326fd917b`. Build toward one immutable quality-proven champion plus exact reversible task specialists; use trained base-bound deltas first and standalone distilled specialists when evidence demands them. Keep explicit fallback routing, composition-bound KV, and separate logical, incremental, standalone, and physical byte accounting. Treat Colibri as native placement research for trained MoE modules, not permission to slice dense models.
current_champion_specialist_submodel_research_anchor: Read `docs/report-intake/2026-07-21/champion-specialist-submodel-research/MANIFEST.md`, its corrected synthesis and TDD delta, and `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-champion-specialist-submodel-research-intake-memory-2026-07-21.md`, SHA256 `c976b9571e945749814274bf086d9af094d9e593ddc46ef5dddb29348bcaa0b6`. Thirteen exact artifacts close the assignment with twelve reports in six paired lanes. Build one immutable champion plus direct reversible identity-bound specialists, use standalone distillation when adapters fail measured needs, route before generation with champion fallback, flush composition-bound KV, and count every byte class. Colibri may inform compatible trained-MoE placement only. Arbitrary slicing, destructive cumulative mutation, hidden retries, unreviewed training, and report-derived quality or performance claims remain forbidden.
current_turbovec_turboquant_research_anchor: Read `docs/report-intake/2026-07-18/turbovec-turboquant-and-handoff-audit/MANIFEST.md`, the synthesis and TDD delta beside it, and `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-turbovec-turboquant-intake-memory-2026-07-18.md`, SHA256 `0632d3c3cbe6be1326a83f725f8f501000c9b76a9bc1c6d9f79944e5aaf64d3f`. Preserve weight, KV-cache, and durable-index format separation; source-pin first; build scalar numerical oracles; measure equal-byte native/WASM accuracy, recall, memory, and tails; and keep every adoption, speedup, bit-width, and quality claim unpromoted until local receipts pass.
current_exact_flat_retrieval_foundation_anchor: Read `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-exact-flat-retrieval-foundation-memory-2026-07-21.md`, SHA256 `6a0f3241253b1d666959984869c4ec29eb04c97fb67a446ccdb89bc26423de76`; preregistration SHA256 is `0d9b6b3d31a25cba843034ceeafca3a88bc1287546f66025b62d13ba14441152`, ledger SHA256 is `7daa7653222914a028e636e6de6e195f94cb5eb50d5bd10a76af624877303808`, and child receipt `exact-flat-retrieval-75f95baa316315ea` SHA256 is `893e96f461f701f46a3aaaeecddd67bc2b700625ccdb9f0d83ce4b0b67d8c18c`. The immutable scalar receipt remains its parent, while separate browser and named-target children now prove exact test-module execution and bounded host measurements. This foundation grants no TurboVec parity, compression, representative retrieval quality, durable on-disk deletion, product, training, or release authority.
preserved_turbovec_turboquant_deeper_research_handoff: The six standalone assignments are preserved at `docs/report-intake/2026-08-08/active-handoff-closure/2026-07-18-six-disconnected-turbovec-turboquant-deeper-performance-accuracy-research-prompts.md`, SHA256 `d4f74fec15cd0c0cb4d3511bb3e310fe9a3f2b5ba9421d37f490118b76a9262c`. They are no longer active intake. The lanes remain useful research provenance, but prompt prose and returned prose cannot promote a dependency, format, speedup, bit width, recall, quality, browser, or adoption claim. Any new compressed arm requires a new preregistration and objective local evidence.
current_dogfood_campaign_anchor: Current execution authority is `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-dogfood-quality-campaign-execution-memory-2026-07-15.md`, SHA256 `306417b98ca8f18deef909bee9fd4cfacdcb097d2601bc30b90ab65a820f8638`. Dashboard v8 is healthy, resumable, and honestly incomplete with 64 terminal candidate rejections, 14 blockers, 17/24 fault cases, a clean 625-artifact public scan under `sha256:14864479a4ad763c03bbb71b29c727e95d59172572c57482569247ca3f8e46b8`, and unsigned incomplete attestation `sha256:f791579755a521f0fa86b1726a55c4c45f0bf1ca240f461224dc2b4892db8763`. Qualified models remain 0/20, deletion-backed browser rounds 0/50, authorized live MemoryEndpoints continuity runs 0/25, outside lane proofs 0/40, and catalog announcements 0/20. This session is not connected to MemoryEndpoints.com and has validated no individual account. WIP commit `15bcf5049eb8616f856daf8cbc8604b877a7af0b` tracks third-party model weights and remains a release blocker pending explicit owner-authorized cleanup and Git-object audit. Preserve immutable failure history, exactly two total P2P lane processes, cryptographic release authorization, the pre-release no-debt/no-legacy rule, and zero live claims from local or incomplete evidence.
current_croissantllmchat_source_anchor: Exact public `croissantllm/CroissantLLMChat-v0.1` revision `f05665c340c868ce48cebdf997cfafb7dbfef2b3` is terminally rejected at 2/8 under current receipt `sha256:d3aa3d7404a01c4e1ac6bb812bc926b62c8d91f3c98d68d5d78c5878e148c518`. The publisher card authorizes tokenizer EOS 32000 while the generation sidecar declares EOS 2; schema v4 and recorder v11 bind the immutable README and `[32000]` explicitly instead of silently choosing. The exact dense full-MHA source failed completion, ambiguity, practical constraints, balanced lawful-adult analysis, and untrusted-memory precedence. Do not convert, adapt, quantize, package, catalog, or build compatibility for it. Read `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-croissantllmchat-v0.1-source-screen-memory-2026-07-18.md`, SHA256 `15ab70d7adbf0595f8fb7479907669639df6904dea0aade06a2639ee0460bb67`.
current_preference_training_provenance_anchor: The frozen 100-record Qwen3 cognitive-liberty SFT corpus contains 56 edited and 44 unchanged reviewed responses, but zero explicit pairwise decisions and zero eligible preference pairs. The machine audit is `artifacts/training/qwen3-cognitive-liberty-v3/preference-provenance-audit-v1.json`, SHA256 `a9b9bffb58d245d8f23174446f9b088be0d0190e2f33df4cd102cd2212e694d9`; the public-safe report is `artifacts/reports/qwen3-cognitive-liberty-v3-preference-provenance-audit.md`, SHA256 `92eb49863f96b36baa21419766b3d2715de1318d982432f1bef030a1f2fcb19f`. Agent review does not authorize DPO, ORPO, or any inferred preference objective. Require explicit hash-bound human pairwise review; the separate 42-record role-history and 668-record expanded Qwen2.5 handoffs remain 0 resolved and have no training authority.
current_deeper_small_model_research_anchor: Read `docs/report-intake/2026-07-15/deeper-small-model-research/MANIFEST.md` and `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-deeper-small-model-research-intake-synthesis-2026-07-15.md`, SHA256 `e16005831c42a75c7dd57b4334702438c73afc5c89bdaa616b6a1db63b9e4a43`. The twelve paired reports support stronger tests and research methods, not an immediate hybrid rewrite: exact LFM2.5-1.2B remains rejected at 4/8. Require individual data review, trusted contamination exclusion, measured quantization arms, immutable preregistration, and the 24-case fault gate; reject unsupported equations, universal methods, and unreviewed training data.
anchors:
  - Runtime.MiRust.com branding only for project documentation.
  - Zero-third-party-crate runtime and packer policy remains protected.
  - `.uai` hot memory and wiki/runtime-mirust durable reports stay checksum-bound.
  - Safetensors-to-browser evidence remains review-gated, source-bound, eval-bound, and selector-admitted.
  - TinyRustLM.com is the pre-release local-run product surface; Runtime.MiRust.com remains documentation and evidence; SLMComposer.com is retired historical naming.
long_term_goals:
  - Make optional MemoryEndpoints continuity complete for accountless TinyRustLM browser clients through the live 12-record virtual-UAIX contract, explicit revision conflicts, durable cursor check-ins, cross-device recovery, and zero persisted credentials while preserving local `.uai` authority where available.
  - Make local `.slm` conversation and common-sense results genuinely useful while keeping explicit compact and optional quality footprint tiers.
  - Replace whole-file main-thread model copies with exact preflight and bounded OPFS/worker loading, mediated network policy, cross-browser capability fallbacks, and atomic last-known-good runtime rollback.
  - Govern assistant behavior by the UAIX Cognitive Liberty Charter: lawful adult agency and direct help by default, with only narrow transparent concrete-harm boundaries.
  - Grow `.slm` adoption through MiniModel.org metadata and the TinyRustLM P2P network without exposing proprietary conversion, training, ranking, optimization, or commercial internals.
  - Treat Hugging Face as an optional future public mirror for approved `.slm` artifacts, manifests, checksums, license notices, and usage metadata; it is not the product authority or current publishing destination.
  - Never publish rejected adapters, raw teacher drafts, private evaluations, proprietary recipes, credentials, or unapproved model artifacts.
  - Notify the human before any Hugging Face publication when a candidate has passed license review, fixed and seeded behavior gates, source-to-quantized parity, native and browser runtime tests, package metadata review, and release signing; never publish automatically.
current_owned_streaming_conversation_authority: Remote ownership-taking streaming and exact 970 MB Qwen2.5 q4 browser load/free pass with exact-prefix reuse remain historical evidence. The current local picker uses 4 MiB bounded slices, one exact final WASM allocation, Rust-owned incremental SHA-256 and TinyRustLM checksum state, and a 1 GiB maximum; the mapped-root smoke proves that path with the deterministic 8.6 KiB fixture, so larger local-picker feasibility remains unclaimed pending explicit execution. Read `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-owned-streaming-conversation-memory-2026-07-12.md`, SHA256 `d5033ef3e0343cf51366e8bff384414f9a2c1fe9eb7fc337075c29ea5cbbcf6f`, then the current runtime architecture authority.
current_production_conversation_authority: TinyRustLM.com is now local-or-companion only and no project domain hosts `.slm` bytes. The secure loopback companion can import, receipt-verify, stream, and chat with the real 969648576-byte Qwen artifact; MiniModel.org exposes metadata with zero active peers until genuine outside-network proof exists. The locked visual language remains intact and active chat has one response renderer. Read `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-web-companion-production-memory-2026-07-13.md`, SHA256 `ea8c1633e92e9b119840615ee25e0448f356c69f0d8c3def8172a262576bff3b`.
current_q4_simd_acceleration_authority: Native AVX2 q4 prefill is about 8.0x faster on the controlled probe with identical argmax/top-32 and near-identical logits. Independently manifested scalar/SIMD128 WASM, checksum rejection, owned 970 MB browser loading, and coherent two-turn generation now pass both locally and on public HTTPS. Read `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-q4-simd-acceleration-memory-2026-07-12.md`, SHA256 `8888249c695d5c72132b3b9e069c1b37324799048254e663588720dbfbb07c0a`, then the production conversation authority.
current_browser_performance_authority: Exact complete-prefix KV reuse and optimized portable q4 prefill reduce a controlled local repeated-turn run by 82.75% without changing strict output bytes. The runtime is deployed; a production local-file run exposed an exact-prefix miss after visible-response re-tokenization. This remains performance evidence, not model-quality promotion. Read `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-browser-prefix-cache-performance-memory-2026-07-12.md`, SHA256 `34028b8c0b057733a5ff7e75590e4f9a8caa945e1e4be0b52e013965f8e9769c`.
current_quality_strategy: Qwen2.5-0.5B source and its 100-record sequence/top-k adapters are rejected; exact Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct revision 989aa7980e4cf806f80c7fef2b1adb7bc71aa306 is also rejected at 2/8 and is no longer an anchor. Same-tokenizer top-k and resumable teacher collection work, but infrastructure success is not model promotion. The local Qwen3.6 teacher produced 572 public plus 96 targeted validated drafts. Agent inspection covers all 668 through 428 proposed rewrites, 14 proposed redundant-row rejections, and 226 retained originals. Their exact evidence and both semantic views remain in 27 hash-bound human-review batches with manifest SHA256 `fb4d9da0124e796a08de182a722317d6d83bc47dace9714644b64ff26e0d84df`. Shared progress/final validation proves the initial decision set is pristine at 0/668 resolved and merge readiness false; progress report SHA256 is `3c92135fb4129b9f31fe2c33c02ed51966785e6ea720bf53952947b38a6ab820`. Use the loopback-only explicit review workstation routed through `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-human-review-workstation-memory-2026-07-12.md`; never bulk-approve or infer human judgment. Review every record explicitly, audit each checkpoint without text disclosure, merge only at zero pending, export and freeze only approved output, compare matched sequence/top-k candidates, convert only a genuinely distinct passing source, and choose mixed precision through measured sensitivity. Existing Qwen conversion, deployment, or training code has no compatibility authority under the standing pre-release no-debt/no-legacy rule. Authority routes are the current Qwen2.5 source-screen report, human-review workstation memory, agent-assisted review memory, v12 progress assessment and hosted receipt, v20 pending and v20/v21 semantic audit receipts, distillation durable memory, and small-model batch-2 memory.
current_single_use_agent_enrollment_authority: TinyRustLM accepts one secret invitation URL, claims it atomically once, clears it, and returns a canonical agreed agent name plus agent-scoped token. Clean-browser recovery uses only name+token and must restore the same virtual-UAIX short/long memory. Same-key retry is original-operation recovery; distinct-key URL reuse must be dead. Every test creates disposable authority that must be closed and deleted even after failure. Production currently lacks the advertised capability, so implementation remains blocked and backend defects are posted; local control-flow fixtures pass. Read `docs/architecture/memory-endpoints-single-use-agent-enrollment-tdd-plan.md`, SHA256 `95a7cec63a775d0c5fac83f78ecbb4e7244e6195e8d692ad9df437c5a596c553`.
current_conversation_quality_authority: The strict seven-case one-call gate keeps exact role history and untouched greedy output; no candidate is promoted for that broader strict-quality scope. Separately, the optional public Qwen route is admitted only to the narrower conversation-proven tier after real two-turn HTTPS proof and remains `qualityCapable=false`. Preserve the strict fixture as a training exclusion and improve conflict confirmation, untrusted-memory precedence, and feasible fallback behavior through reviewed role-history work. Read `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-multi-turn-conversation-memory-2026-07-12.md`, SHA256 `9e8e8d909a1a073e4e5fca3667f2463eeffc8be806abdf8c2817fb3838f10c79`, then the production conversation authority.
current_role_history_distillation_authority: Role-preserving import, freeze, collection/export, and trainer tokenization are implemented and verified for one to six complete prior turns. The 42-record campaign remains 0/42 human-resolved and has no training authority. Public-safe MemoryEndpoints status/handoff are promoted and tier-isolated. Never bulk-approve, train, promote, convert, publish, or deploy it before explicit review, merge/export, contamination-safe freeze, unchanged strict evaluation, and regression gates. Read `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-role-history-distillation-memory-2026-07-12.md`, SHA256 `1d55ce8ea235ef58a345f1f4489159de4c85100027e2b0502d5bc1e71bd9bb9d`.
current_quantization_fidelity_authority: Native f32 Qwen3-0.6B parity is exact; `mixed-q8-matrix-f32-norm-v1` is the current compact fidelity profile at 602,862,400 bytes and 7/7 substantive source argmax, but the source model remains assistant-quality-pending. Read `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-qwen3-0.6b-quantization-fidelity-memory-2026-07-12.md`, SHA256 `00216ebfbfd5c5b822446fff999614882b94ed6b58ddaaf1a74bdb1cdd3d393f`, before conversion, performance, selection, or quality claims.
current_runtime_architecture_authority: The 13 MemoryEndpoints Rust/WASM pages remain proposed/reviewed. Current sampler behavior rejects NaN/+infinity, reserves -infinity for suppression, and fails collapsed distributions. Remote and local-picker model bytes can enter one owned WASM allocation up to 1 GiB; local picker input is read in bounded slices and digest identity is finalized in Rust before runtime adoption. OPFS/worker loading, artifacts beyond 1 GiB, scale-offset parsing, and broader large-artifact fault-injection evidence remain open. Read `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-rust-wasm-architecture-coverage-memory-2026-07-12.md`, SHA256 `e84eb43fb31f6f4e2af8dc0e3115daf13a3cebef40e6a980cc2852e88a744d22`, then the owned-streaming authority.
current_human_review_workstation_authority: `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-human-review-workstation-memory-2026-07-12.md`, SHA256 `a4c8bcb67fadb7e3bf577869db0458e561af473d9b5c0d486c7811020721edd6`.
current_dotnet_p2p_seed_host_authority: Read `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-web-companion-production-memory-2026-07-13.md` (SHA256 `ea8c1633e92e9b119840615ee25e0448f356c69f0d8c3def8172a262576bff3b`) for current version 0.1.10 bridge, local-feed, RID, deployment, browser, test, and release truth, then the corrected intake plan for rationale. Preserve exactly two total lane processes for up to 20 models, Rust trust authority, direct peer bytes, external proof, no persisted credentials, protected APIs, and transactional history. Never turn local health or local publication into a claim of public reachability, NuGet.org publication, production signing, or installed service state. The companion is operational P2P infrastructure, not a second chat UI.
